  "notes": [
    "Six strong card poses occupy twelve keyed frames through explicit two-key holds.",
    "Card bodies copy exact accepted starter_blade_accents_002b1 native cels and the accepted bit/ratchet parts, without resizing or recolouring.",
    "Rank II develops physical force and travel marks rather than adding a device.",
    "Icons are separately authored recognizable miniature tops and travel/contact.",
    "FX omit replacement bodies, gadgets and synthetic particles; real gameplay tops remain visible.",
    "All eight projected headings have eight authored native keys. Existing gameplay fields/events remain authoritative.",
    "The accepted broad round Bastion body replaces the smaller angular Vane as the foreground braking subject, at its original native pixel scale.",
    "Stored key zero is empty. Positive keys one through seven retain a short bright folded floor skid behind the actual heel even at low earned charge; greater charge tightens it. Rank II adds one second fold. No free-running charge animation.",
    "Final stored folds use individually directed upright rear spans per heading and a continuous short floor seam back to the actual bit, so the live native blade cannot occlude the hold. Store and release cels are unchanged."
  ],
